{"seq":31,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24722"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-022, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Agronomy] Which of the following crops are NOT part of the “Three Sisters” intercropping technique used by Native Americans?\nA. Wild rice\nB. Beans\nC. Squash\nAnswer: A. The “Three Sisters” refers to the intercropping of maize, beans, and squash, a companion planting method used by Native American tribes to enhance soil fertility and crop yields: Maize provides a structure for the beans to climb, beans fix nitrogen in the soil to benefit all three plants, and squash spreads along the ground, blocking sunlight to prevent weeds and retaining moisture in the soil.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-022.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which three crops are grown together in the “Three Sisters” intercropping technique of Native Americans?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welche drei Nutzpflanzen werden bei der „Drei Schwestern“-Mischkultur der amerikanischen Ureinwohner zusammen angebaut?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-022","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Agronomy] Which of the following crops are NOT part of the “Three Sisters” intercropping technique used by Native Americans?\nA. Wild rice\nB. Beans\nC. Squash\nAnswer: A. The “Three Sisters” refers to the intercropping of maize, beans, and squash, a companion planting method used by Native American tribes to enhance soil fertility and crop yields: Maize provides a structure for the beans to climb, beans fix nitrogen in the soil to benefit all three plants, and squash spreads along the ground, blocking sunlight to prevent weeds and retaining moisture in the soil."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f02514"}],"hash":"190b79caea60"},
